s containing one simile and  no  metaphors the  mabinogian and the norse sagas are as  plain spoken as could well be clarity  and simplicity are permanent virtues in  a narrative a plain language  is the noblest of all so if we're going  to depart from plain language it has to  come organically it has to fit it cannot  be something put on for the marketplace  right or to imitate and thereby win  ourselves a place in the fantasy  pantheon because fantasy is one of those  things where  true greatness winds up being recognized  by people and mediocrity also winds up  being recognized despite the number of  book sales by  looking where people keep going back  right we keep still reading  tolkien  and leguin  and vance  and some of these other authors as well  so a lot of important themes running  through elf land to poughkeepsie there's  nothing wrong with with poughkeepsie  she's not saying get rid of it  but elfland has to  stand on its own in literary works  and we don't want poughkeepsie  becoming the model  for  elfland or elfland ceases to be  what it is  you
 

